e path points to a directory writable by the attacker. DHI Alpine images do not ship such fstab entries and do not invoke mount(8) loop-device setup during normal operation.","justification":"vulnerable_code_cannot_be_controlled_by_adversary","timestamp":"2026-07-28T20:02:32.911Z"},{"@id":"f370e76b-1035-476e-8d61-cb4bc808f32e","vulnerability":{"name":"CVE-2026-1757"},"products":[{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1"},{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1?os_name=alpine\u0026os_version=3.22"},{"@id":"pkg:docker/dhi/composer","subcomponents":[{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1?os_name=alpine\u0026os_version=3.22"}]},{"@id":"pkg:oci/composer?repository_url=dhi.io","subcomponents":[{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1"}]},{"@id":"pkg:oci/dhi.io%2Fcomposer","subcomponents":[{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1"}]}],"status":"under_investigation","status_notes":"Memory leak in the xmllint interactive shell when the input line contains only whitespace. The DHI libxml2 APK backports the upstream fix for rebuilt r2 (3.23) and r3 (3.24) releases; stock Alpine PURLs remain under investigation until consumers pick up the DHI rebuild. Reference: https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-1757","timestamp":"2026-07-07T23:04:24.737Z"},{"@id":"ce6aa188-9120-4571-86db-fc76c419fad3","vulnerability":{"name":"CVE-2026-11979"},"products":[{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1"},{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1?os_name=alpine\u0026os_version=3.22"},{"@id":"pkg:docker/dhi/composer","subcomponents":[{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1?os_name=alpine\u0026os_version=3.22"}]},{"@id":"pkg:oci/composer?repository_url=dhi.io","subcomponents":[{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1"}]},{"@id":"pkg:oci/dhi.io%2Fcomposer","subcomponents":[{"@id":"pkg:apk/alpine/libxml2@2.13.9-r1"}]}],"status":"under_investigation","status_notes":"Stack buffer overflows in the xmlcatalog interactive shell (--shell) usershell() parser in upstream Alpine libxml2 2.13.9